# cmd.exe mis-parses batch files that use bare LF line endings, so our linker
# script must be CRLF wherever it is checked out.
#
# Scoped to tools/ deliberately: upstream commits its own .bat files (waf.bat,
# utils/makefont/CreateFont.bat) with CRLF bytes already in the blob, so a bare
# "*.bat text eol=crlf" would report them as modified forever.  On top of the
# noise in "git status", game_shared/CMakeLists.txt runs
# "git describe --dirty" at configure time and compiles the result into both
# game libraries, so that would bake a "-dirty" revision into every release.
tools/*.bat text eol=crlf
